Controls what happens when a bounded channel is full and a producer attempts to write.
| `Wait`       | `WriteAsync` blocks until space is available                     | Default. Reliable delivery with back-pressure        |
Multiple producers can call `WriteAsync` or `TryWrite` concurrently on a shared channel without external locking.
A `Channel<T>` is a thread-safe producer/consumer structure with separate `ChannelWriter<T>` and `ChannelReader<T>` endpoints; the channel handles synchronization.
With the `System.Linq.Async` NuGet package, channel streams can be composed with async LINQ operators such as `Where` and `Buffer`.
`BoundedChannelFullMode.DropWrite` drops the item being written when the channel is full; the guide presents it for non-blocking writes where overflow should be detected or tracked.
`BoundedChannelFullMode.DropNewest` drops the newest item in the channel when full; the guide associates it with discarding excess incoming work.
`BoundedChannelFullMode.DropOldest` drops the oldest queued item to make room for new data; it suits telemetry or metrics where recent readings matter more than stale ones.

